# Rank 1525 / CVE-2026-34717: OpenProject's reporting =n operator
# interpolated a user-supplied number string straight into its SQL
# WHERE clause, so a crafted filter value injected SQL (SQL injection,
# CWE-89; GHSA-5rrm-6qmq-2364, patched in 17.2.3; the task list's
# nocommit flag reflects advisory-side absence -- the advisory names the
# file and line, and the fixing commit fixes exactly that line). The
# operator block in modules/reporting/lib/report/operator.rb did
# `def modify(query, field, value); query.where "#{field} =
# #{parse_number_string(value)}"; query; end` -- field and value
# arrive from the report filter (request parameters through the
# query builder), and the string interpolation bypasses every
# placeholder. The fixing commit (confirmed --
# "Correctly evaluate parse number string in =n operator"): the where
# call becomes the array form `query.where ["#{field} = ?",
# parse_number_string_to_number(value)]` -- placeholder
# parameterisation plus a numeric-coercion helper. No pool
# correction.
#
# CAUGHT by VYQL-INJ-001. The ruby path rule covers the shape end to
# end: modify's parameters are labelled code.ExternalEntryInput by
# library.param-source, the interpolated query.where is the
# code.SqlExecution sink, and the array form is credited as
# core.SqlParameterization. Measured on the real code: at the fixed revision
# parent operator.rb carries ten INJ-001 HIGH rows (:96 :111 :119
# :123 :132 :177 :206 :234 :240 :244 -- the file's other operators
# interpolate the same way), and at the fixed revision the row on :177 -- the
# advisory's exact line -- is gone while the nine untouched operators
# keep reporting: the rule discriminates the parameterised form from
# the interpolated one in the real file. No definition change
# shipped, no benchmark impact. Spec cve_rank1525 records the
# interpolated =n expecting VYQL-INJ-001 and the array-form rejecting
# it.

test "rank1525: the number operator interpolates its value"
  lang ruby
  file modules/reporting/lib/report/operator.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  class Report::FilterController < ApplicationController
    def apply
      field = params[:f]
      value = params[:v]

      query = Report::Query.new
      query.where "#{field} = #{parse_number_string(value)}"
      render json: query.all
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1525: the fixed revision parameterises the comparison"
  lang ruby
  file modules/reporting/lib/report/operator.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  class Report::FilterController < ApplicationController
    def apply
      field = params[:f]
      value = params[:v]

      query = Report::Query.new
      query.where ["#{field} = ?", parse_number_string_to_number(value)]
      render json: query.all
    end
  end
  ```
